{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsdY2EJ7kZ6Ko59P6FMx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled R30F1 **FIX**. Round 9's half-finished coprocess rule both lets a model launch go unread and wrongly blocks a harmless command. The verdict is committed as `2d69106e` in `docs/reviews/wi-834/031-ADJUDICATE-6e90615.md`, with the `WI: WI-834` trailer.\n\n**What I reproduced:**\n- **Allowed, but should be denied:** `coproc WORK while claude …`, `coproc WORK if codex …` and `coproc WORK until claude …`. The hook reads `work` as the command.\n- **Denied, but runs no model:** `coproc CLAUDE while true; …`, which reads `claude`. The baseline did not have this false denial.\n- **Already correct:** the `{`, `for`, `(`, unnamed and plain-command coprocess forms.\n- **Real Bash:** a named coprocess runs its `while` condition, and a coprocess named `CLAUDE` just printed `ok`.\n\nThe cause is the table entry at `coordinator_guard.py:901`. It treats a coprocess NAME as a label only when `{` follows. Bash's grammar puts an optional NAME before any compound command (`while`, `if`, `until`, `for` and so on).\n\n**Why FIX despite the rarity:** the builder concedes named coprocesses are rare in agent commands. Two things decide it:\n- These are Bash grammar, not wrappers. The model CLI is the command word in the loop or `if` condition, so this falls inside the coverage line I drew in sitting 025.\n- The lane itself wrote this rule in round 9 and only did half of it, creating both the gap and a new false denial. Finishing that one table cell, plus three TC-339 tests, costs less than the inconsistency it removes.\n\nThe builder's noted residual is acceptable: `coproc NAME ( … )` still reads NAME as the command because the reader splits at `(`, but it still reads the body and over-denies only a coprocess named after a model CLI.\n\nTo help close this recurring class, the verdict adds a rule for later rounds: once this cell is fixed, the reader covers Bash's coprocess grammar fully. Any further grammar-only form that no ordinary agent writes, and that the lane did not just introduce, belongs with the line-continuation trick dismissed in sitting 005, not another review round.\n\nMy probe scripts are in the session scratchpad. The `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3048,"cache_read_input_tokens":522986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3048},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"bfe0a7db-b06c-45f9-91e0-bb6347c44931","timestamp":"2026-10-10T00:44:22.239Z","request_id":"req_011CfsdY1wB69RRwfFhdQ4M8"}
